#### Project-local xschemrc for OSBCIChip/xschem
#### SkyWater 130 PDK configuration

#### Set the Sky130 PDK root to the volare-installed PDK.
#### This directory must contain the `sky130A/` (or `sky130B/`) process directory.
set env(PDK_ROOT) /Users/noah/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/0fe599b2afb6708d281543108caf8310912f54af

#### Select the process variant: sky130A (default) or sky130B
set env(PDK) sky130A

#### Point xschem to the local source tree so standard device symbols
#### (vsource, gnd, capa, lab_pin, code_shown, ...) are found.
#### NOTE: leave XSCHEM_SHAREDIR to xschem's auto-detection. Setting it to
#### the bare source root breaks init (xschem.tcl lives in src/), which
#### aborts xschemrc processing and loses the sky130 symbol libraries.
#### set XSCHEM_SHAREDIR /Users/noah/xschem

#### Source the PDK-provided xschemrc. This loads the symbol libraries,
#### device colors, DRC procedures, and SKYWATER_MODELS / SKYWATER_STDCELLS variables.
source $env(PDK_ROOT)/$env(PDK)/libs.tech/xschem/xschemrc

#### The PDK xschemrc resets XSCHEM_LIBRARY_PATH and assumes the standard
#### xschem_library lives under $XSCHEM_SHAREDIR. In this source-tree build
#### (/Users/noah/xschem) the library is a sibling of src/, so re-add it,
#### otherwise basic devices (vsource, gnd, capa, lab_pin, ...) go missing.
append XSCHEM_LIBRARY_PATH :/Users/noah/xschem/xschem_library/devices
append XSCHEM_LIBRARY_PATH :/Users/noah/xschem/xschem_library

#### Uncomment the next line to open the project's schematic on startup.
#### Otherwise xschem starts with an empty schematic when launched from here.
# set XSCHEM_START_WINDOW {1samp.sch}

#### If you prefer the PDK welcome page with example circuits, comment out
#### the line below. The welcome page is useful when learning the PDK symbols.
unset XSCHEM_START_WINDOW
